  "generated": false,
  "title": "Emotional Dysregulation Therapy | Michelle Barratt Psychology",
  "description": "Some children and teenagers experience emotions very intensely.",
  "html": "<!--$--><section class=\"bg-gradient-to-br from-plum to-rose text-white\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20\"><div><nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"mb-6\"><ol class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-white/75\"><li><a class=\"hover:text-white\" href=\"/\">Home</a></li><li aria-hidden=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"></path></svg></li><li><a class=\"hover:text-white\" href=\"/therapy-services\">Therapy Services</a></li><li aria-hidden=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"></path></svg></li><li class=\"text-white\" aria-current=\"page\">Emotional Dysregulation Therapy</li></ol></nav><p class=\"text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-white/85 mb-3\">Children &amp; Adolescent Therapy</p><h1 class=\"text-white text-[32px] md:text-[44px] font-semibold leading-[1.08] max-w-3xl\">Emotional Dysregulation Therapy</h1><div class=\"h-[3px] w-16 bg-sun my-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><div class=\"mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 btn-black-yellow \" href=\"/contact\">Contact Us</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 border border-white/70 text-white hover:bg-white/10 \" href=\"/practitioners\">See Practitioners</a></div></div></div></section><section id=\"helping-your-child-or-teenager-understand-and-manage-big-emo\" class=\"bg-white \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">Helping Your Child or Teenager Understand and Manage Big Emotions</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Some children and teenagers experience emotions very intensely.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">They may become overwhelmed quickly, have difficulty calming down after becoming upset, react strongly to situations that seem small to others, or find it difficult to put their feelings into words.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">For parents, it can be difficult to know what is behind these reactions or how best to respond.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Emotional regulation is a skill that can be developed.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Therapy can help children and teenagers understand their emotional experiences, recognise what is happening before emotions become overwhelming, and develop strategies for responding in ways that better support their wellbeing and relationships.</p><nav class=\"toc\" aria-labelledby=\"toc-title\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"toc-toggle\" data-toc-toggle aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"toc-list\"><span id=\"toc-title\" class=\"toc-title\">On This Page</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"toc-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></button><ol id=\"toc-list\" class=\"toc-list\"><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#helping-your-child-or-teenager-understand-and-manage-big-emo\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Helping Your Child or Teenager Understand and Manage Big Emotions</span></a></li><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#what-is-emotional-dysregulation\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>What Is Emotional Dysregulation?</span></a></li><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#when-big-feelings-become-hard-to-manage\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>When Big Feelings Become Hard to Manage</span></a></li><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#what-can-contribute-to-emotional-dysregulation\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>What Can Contribute to Emotional Dysregulation?</span></a></li><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#emotional-dysregulation-and-adhd\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Emotional Dysregulation and ADHD</span></a></li><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#you-may-be-looking-for-support-because\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>You May Be Looking for Support Because...</span></a></li><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#how-can-therapy-help\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>How Can Therapy Help?</span></a></li><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#what-about-dbt\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>What About DBT?</span></a></li><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#for-parents-you-can-help-your-child-learn-regulation\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>For Parents: You Can Help Your Child Learn Regulation</span></a></li><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#what-could-change-with-the-right-support\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>What Could Change With the Right Support?</span></a></li><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#when-should-you-seek-professional-support\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>When Should You Seek Professional Support?</span></a></li><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#you-dont-need-to-know-where-to-start\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>You Don't Need to Know Where to Start</span></a></li><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#why-families-choose-mbp\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Why Families Choose MBP</span></a></li><li><a class=\"toc-link\" href=\"#start-with-a-conversation\"><span class=\"toc-dot h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Start With a Conversation</span></a></li></ol></nav></div></section><section id=\"what-is-emotional-dysregulation\" class=\"bg-soft \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">What Is Emotional Dysregulation?</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Emotion regulation refers to the ability to influence and manage our emotional state. This does not mean preventing emotions or never becoming upset.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Everyone experiences anger, frustration, sadness, anxiety and excitement.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">The difficulty can arise when emotions become so intense, persistent or difficult to manage that they begin affecting everyday life, relationships, learning or participation in activities.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Emotional dysregulation can look different from one person to another.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">A child or teenager may:</p><ul class=\"max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Become overwhelmed quickly</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Have intense emotional reactions</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Move rapidly from one emotion to another</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Struggle to calm down after becoming upset</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>React impulsively when emotions are strong</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Find it difficult to identify or describe what they are feeling</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Become frustrated when things do not go as expected</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Become stuck in repetitive negative thinking</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Withdraw when emotionally overwhelmed</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Find conflict particularly difficult</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Regret things they have said or done after becoming calmer</span></li></ul><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">These experiences do not automatically mean a child has a mental health disorder.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Understanding what is driving the difficulty is an important part of assessment and treatment.</p></div></section><section id=\"when-big-feelings-become-hard-to-manage\" class=\"bg-white \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">When Big Feelings Become Hard to Manage</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">A child might cope well most of the time but become overwhelmed when they are tired, stressed, disappointed, frustrated or faced with an unexpected change.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">For another child, emotional regulation difficulties may occur more frequently and affect school, friendships or family life.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">You may notice:</p><h3 class=\"text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3\">At home</h3><ul class=\"max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Frequent emotional outbursts</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Difficulty accepting limits or changes</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Arguments that escalate quickly</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Difficulty moving on after becoming upset</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Needing significant support to calm down</span></li></ul><h3 class=\"text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3\">At school</h3><ul class=\"max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Difficulty managing frustration</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Emotional reactions to mistakes or perceived criticism</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Problems concentrating when emotionally overwhelmed</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Conflict with peers or teachers</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Difficulty transitioning between activities</span></li></ul><h3 class=\"text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3\">With friendships</h3><ul class=\"max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Strong reactions to disagreements</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Difficulty interpreting social situations</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Impulsive responses during conflict</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Feeling rejected or misunderstood</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Difficulty repairing relationships after an emotional reaction</span></li></ul></div></section><section id=\"what-can-contribute-to-emotional-dysregulation\" class=\"bg-soft \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"grid gap-10 photo-fill\"><div class=\"min-w-0 photo-fill-text\"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">What Can Contribute to Emotional Dysregulation?</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Emotional regulation difficulties can have many possible contributors.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">They may be associated with:</p><ul class=\"max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Stress or significant life changes</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Anxiety or persistent worry</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Difficulties with attention or impulse control</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>ADHD symptoms</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Neurodevelopmental differences</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Challenges with identifying or expressing emotions</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Sleep difficulties</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Difficulties in relationships or social situations</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Experiences that have been emotionally overwhelming</span></li></ul><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">The relationship between emotional regulation and ADHD is particularly relevant for some young people. Current ACAMH guidance notes that adolescents with ADHD symptoms may experience intense or rapidly changing emotions, strong emotional reactions and emotionally driven behaviours.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">However, emotional dysregulation is not the same thing as ADHD, and a child's presentation should be considered individually.</p></div><img src=\"/images/stock/pexels-7820626.webp\" alt=\"An upset young child holding an adult's hand\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"photo-fill-img w-full object-cover rounded-lg border border-lilac\"/></div></div></section><section id=\"emotional-dysregulation-and-adhd\" class=\"bg-white \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">Emotional Dysregulation and ADHD</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">For some adolescents with ADHD symptoms, difficulties with emotional regulation can add to the challenges they are already experiencing.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">They may find it difficult to recognise emotions as they arise, shift away from emotionally charged thoughts, pause before reacting, or choose a helpful response when emotions are intense.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">ACAMH's 2026 guidance highlights several skills that may support emotional regulation, including acceptance, cognitive reappraisal, grounding, reducing rumination and learning to tolerate strong emotions without immediately acting on them.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Importantly, the goal is not to make a young person stop having strong emotions.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">It is to help them develop a larger repertoire of ways to respond.</p></div></section><section id=\"you-may-be-looking-for-support-because\" class=\"bg-soft \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">You May Be Looking for Support Because...</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">You may be considering therapy because your child or teenager:</p><ul class=\"max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Seems to have emotions that feel &quot;too big&quot; for the situation</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Becomes overwhelmed easily</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Has frequent conflicts at home or school</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Finds frustration particularly difficult</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Struggles to calm down once upset</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Acts impulsively when emotional</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Has difficulty explaining what they are feeling</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Is experiencing problems with friendships</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Becomes stuck in negative thought patterns</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Is finding everyday situations increasingly difficult to manage</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Has ADHD or ADHD symptoms alongside emotional regulation difficulties</span></li></ul><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">You may also simply have a sense that your child is struggling to manage emotions in ways that are affecting their everyday life.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">You don't need to know the exact reason before seeking support.</p></div></section><section id=\"how-can-therapy-help\" class=\"bg-white \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">How Can Therapy Help?</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Therapy can give a child or teenager a safe space to understand their emotional experiences without being judged for having strong feelings.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Depending on their age and individual needs, therapy may focus on:</p><div class=\"grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 my-8 support-cards\"><div class=\"bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6\"><span class=\"block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><h3 class=\"text-xl font-semibold mb-2\">Recognising emotions</h3><p class=\"text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85\">Learning to notice emotional and physical signs that indicate an emotion is building.</p></div><div class=\"bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6\"><span class=\"block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><h3 class=\"text-xl font-semibold mb-2\">Naming and communicating feelings</h3><p class=\"text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85\">Developing language to explain what they are experiencing and what they need.</p></div><div class=\"bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6\"><span class=\"block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><h3 class=\"text-xl font-semibold mb-2\">Understanding emotional triggers</h3><p class=\"text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85\">Identifying situations, thoughts, relationships or patterns that tend to increase emotional intensity.</p></div><div class=\"bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6\"><span class=\"block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><h3 class=\"text-xl font-semibold mb-2\">Cognitive reappraisal</h3><p class=\"text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85\">Learning to consider alternative or more balanced ways of interpreting emotionally difficult situations. This is commonly incorporated into CBT-based approaches.</p></div><div class=\"bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6\"><span class=\"block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><h3 class=\"text-xl font-semibold mb-2\">Acceptance and mindfulness</h3><p class=\"text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85\">Learning that an emotion can be acknowledged without immediately needing to act on it.</p></div><div class=\"bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6\"><span class=\"block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><h3 class=\"text-xl font-semibold mb-2\">Grounding and attention strategies</h3><p class=\"text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85\">Developing practical ways to reconnect with the present moment when emotions become intense.</p></div><div class=\"bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6\"><span class=\"block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><h3 class=\"text-xl font-semibold mb-2\">Problem-solving and communication</h3><p class=\"text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85\">Building skills for responding to difficult situations, managing disagreements and asking for support.</p></div><div class=\"bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6\"><span class=\"block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><h3 class=\"text-xl font-semibold mb-2\">Building emotional flexibility</h3><p class=\"text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85\">Learning that different situations may require different regulation strategies rather than relying on one response every time.</p></div></div></div></section><section id=\"what-about-dbt\" class=\"bg-soft \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">What About DBT?</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Dialectical Behaviour Therapy (DBT) includes skills relevant to emotional regulation, distress tolerance, mindfulness and interpersonal effectiveness.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">For some adolescents, DBT-informed strategies may form part of psychological therapy when clinically appropriate.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">However, DBT is not automatically appropriate for every child or teenager experiencing emotional dysregulation. The type of therapy should be matched to the young person's individual presentation, developmental stage and treatment needs.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">ACAMH's discussion of DBT for adolescents highlights its relevance to emotion regulation and related difficulties while also considering the developing evidence base and the importance of adapting approaches appropriately for young people.</p></div></section><section id=\"for-parents-you-can-help-your-child-learn-regulation\" class=\"bg-white \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"grid gap-10 photo-fill\"><div class=\"min-w-0 photo-fill-text\"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">For Parents: You Can Help Your Child Learn Regulation</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Children develop emotional regulation partly through their relationships with supportive adults.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Parents can help by:</p><ul class=\"max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Staying as calm as possible when their child is overwhelmed</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Helping the child identify and name emotions</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Acknowledging the feeling without automatically agreeing with every reaction</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Modelling healthy ways of responding to frustration</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Talking about emotions when everyone is calm</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Helping the child recognise patterns and triggers</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Encouraging age-appropriate problem-solving</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Allowing opportunities to practise skills rather than expecting immediate perfection</span></li></ul><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Parents do not have to prevent every difficult emotion.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">The goal is to help children gradually learn:</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">&quot;I can feel this emotion, understand what is happening, and learn what to do next.&quot;</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Psychology Today similarly highlights the role of parents in modelling coping strategies and helping children identify, label and appropriately express emotions.</p></div><img src=\"/images/stock/pexels-6624311.webp\" alt=\"A mother comforting her son on the couch\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"photo-fill-img w-full object-cover rounded-lg border border-lilac\" style=\"object-position:50% 35%\"/></div></div></section><section id=\"what-could-change-with-the-right-support\" class=\"bg-soft \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">What Could Change With the Right Support?</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">With appropriate support, a child or teenager may begin to:</p><ul class=\"max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Understand their emotional responses more clearly</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Recognise emotions earlier</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Identify triggers and patterns</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Develop practical regulation strategies</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Pause before reacting</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Communicate feelings more effectively</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Handle frustration more flexibly</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Manage difficult social situations</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Reduce conflict at home or school</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Recover more effectively after becoming upset</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Build confidence in their ability to cope</span></li></ul><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">The aim is not emotional perfection.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Everyone becomes angry, disappointed, worried or overwhelmed sometimes.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">The goal is to help a young person develop the skills to navigate those experiences more effectively.</p></div></section><section id=\"when-should-you-seek-professional-support\" class=\"bg-white \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">When Should You Seek Professional Support?</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Consider seeking professional support when emotional regulation difficulties are persistent or are beginning to interfere with your child's everyday life.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">This may include difficulties affecting:</p><ul class=\"max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Family relationships</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Friendships</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>School participation</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Learning and concentration</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Emotional wellbeing</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Behaviour</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Confidence</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Daily routines</span></li></ul><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">You do not have to wait until you have a diagnosis or know exactly what is causing the difficulties.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">An appropriate practitioner can help explore what may be contributing to your child's presentation and whether psychological therapy may be helpful.</p></div></section><section id=\"you-dont-need-to-know-where-to-start\" class=\"bg-soft \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">You Don't Need to Know Where to Start</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">As a parent, it can be difficult to know whether your child's emotional reactions are part of normal development, related to stress, connected with ADHD or another concern, or simply something they need help learning to manage.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">You don't need to diagnose the problem before reaching out.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">At MBP, we can help you understand your options and identify an appropriate practitioner based on your child's or teenager's age, presenting concerns and available services.</p></div></section><section id=\"why-families-choose-mbp\" class=\"bg-white \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">Why Families Choose MBP</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">When your child is struggling with emotions, finding the right type of support can feel overwhelming.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">MBP can help families navigate the first steps by:</p><ul class=\"max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Listening to your concerns</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Understanding your child's individual circumstances</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Helping identify appropriate practitioner options</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Considering age and presenting needs</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Helping you understand the referral and intake process</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90\"><span class=\"mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span>Supporting the administrative steps involved in getting started</span></li></ul><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Our role is to make the pathway to appropriate support clearer.</p></div></section><section id=\"start-with-a-conversation\" class=\"bg-soft svc-contact \"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 \"><div class=\"mb-10 max-w-3xl\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold\">Start With a Conversation</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div></div><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">If your child's emotions are becoming difficult to manage and are affecting their relationships, school experience or everyday life, support may help.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">You don't need to figure it out alone.</p><p class=\"max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5\">Start with a conversation with MBP and let us help you understand where to begin.</p><div class=\"mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 btn-black-yellow \" href=\"/contact\">Contact Us</a></div></div></section><div data-mbp=\"related\"></div><section class=\"bg-blush\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-14 md:py-16 text-center\"><p class=\"text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-rose mb-2.5\">Take the first step</p><h2 class=\"text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-semibold leading-[1.1]\">Ready to Take the First Step?</h2><div class=\"h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-4 mx-auto\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><p class=\"mt-5 text-[17px]\">Seeking support can feel overwhelming, but you do not have to navigate life&#x27;s challenges alone. Our administration team can help answer your questions, explain appointment options and connect you with a suitable practitioner.</p><p class=\"mt-3\">Prefer to call? Phone our administration team on <a class=\"text-ocean underline underline-offset-4 font-medium\" href=\"tel:0731850040\">07 3185 0040</a>.</p><div class=\"mt-7 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-rose text-white hover:bg-[#9d2a59] \" href=\"/practitioners\">Book Online</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-ocean text-white hover:bg-[#095a6f] \" href=\"/contact\">Contact Us</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 border border-plum text-plum hover:bg-lilac  active\" href=\"/therapy-services\" data-status=\"active\" aria-current=\"page\">Explore Services</a></div><p class=\"mt-5 text-sm text-ink/70\">If in crisis, please call 000.</p></div></section><!--/$-->"
}
